## Summary

Added a pure-Node `.pptx` text extractor so uploaded slide decks are no longer `binary-unsupported` — the generation/wizard agents now see slide content through the existing `.extracted` sibling mechanism (same pattern as US-124 docx / US-127 pdf).

**Changes:**
- **`src/lib/server/pptx.ts`** (new) — `extractPptxToMarkdown()`. Opens the OOXML zip with `unzipper` (already a dependency), regex-scans `<a:t>` runs grouped by `<a:p>` paragraphs in `ppt/slides/slideN.xml`, orders slides numerically, emits `## Slajd N` sections. Speaker notes resolved via the slide's `_rels` notesSlide relationship and appended. Empty slides skipped; U+0000 stripped for spawn-argv safety. Returns the same `{ok,markdown,…}`/`{ok:false,reason}` shape as the docx/pdf extractors.
- **`src/lib/server/sources.ts`** — `.pptx` added to `EXTRACTABLE_BINARY_EXTS` and the `resolveSourcePathForPrompt` sibling-preference branch (now docx|pdf|pptx); stale docstrings updated.
- **`upload-sources/route.ts`** — POST extracts `.pptx` (failures logged, never block upload); DELETE cleans up the sibling. `moveDraftSourcesToCourse` needed no change (already generic over `<name>.md` siblings).
- **Tests** — new `pptx.test.ts` (3 tests on a 2972-byte inlined jszip fixture: extraction + notes + Polish diacritics, `## Slajd N` ordering + empty-slide skip, non-zip → `ok:false`). The old "marks .pptx as binary-unsupported" test in `sources.test.ts` replaced with the new with/without-sibling behavior, plus two `resolveSourcePathForPrompt` `.pptx` cases.

**Quality:** typecheck ✅, eslint ✅, full `src/lib/server` + upload-sources suite 572/572 ✅. `prd.json` US-213 `passes: true`, committed as `ef7c6bc`.
